# Proofs from the 2018 test suite (PropositionalTests.java) that use the
# quantifier rules UI, EI, UG and EG. The format is described in ../README.md.
#
# Many of these broke the EI or UG restrictions: EI to a constant that is in
# the conclusion, EI to a variable, or UG on a variable that is free in a
# premise. Each one keeps its id in a corrected form, and the proof as it
# was written is kept as an "-as-written" case that must be rejected.

case: copi-a
source: 2018 test copiATest (all humans are mortal; Socrates is human)
problem: {(∀x)(Hx → Mx)//Hs=>Ms}
3. (Hs → Ms) ; 1 UI
4. Ms ; 3,2 MP
expect: valid

case: ui-a
source: 2018 test UIATest
problem: {(∀x)Ax=>Aa}
2. Aa ; 1 UI
expect: valid

case: ui-b
source: 2018 test UIBTest
problem: {(∀x)Axfg=>Avfg}
2. Avfg ; 1 UI
expect: valid

case: ui-c
source: 2018 test UICTest
problem: {(∀x)(∀z)Axzg=>Aazg}
2. (∀z)Aazg ; 1 UI
3. Aazg ; 2 UI
expect: valid

case: ui-d
source: 2018 test UIDTest
problem: {(∀y)(Ey & (∀x)(∀z)Axzy)=>Aabc}
2. Ec & (∀x)(∀z)Axzc ; 1 UI
3. (∀x)(∀z)Axzc & Ec ; 2 COM
4. (∀x)(∀z)Axzc ; 3 SIMP
5. (∀z)Aazc ; 4 UI
6. Aabc ; 5 UI
expect: valid

case: ui-e
source: 2018 test UIETest
problem: {(∀y)((∀y)Ey & (∀x)(∀z)Axzy)=>Aabc}
2. (∀y)Ey & (∀x)(∀z)Axzc ; 1 UI
3. (∀x)(∀z)Axzc & (∀y)Ey ; 2 COM
4. (∀x)(∀z)Axzc ; 3 SIMP
5. (∀z)Aazc ; 4 UI
6. Aabc ; 5 UI
expect: valid

case: ui-f
source: 2018 test UIFTest
problem: {Lhd//(∀x)(Lxd → Lxt)//(∀x)(Lhx → Gx)=>Gt}
4. (Lhd → Lht) ; 2 UI
5. Lht ; 4,1 MP
6. (Lht → Gt) ; 3 UI
7. Gt ; 6,5 MP
expect: valid

case: ei-a
source: 2018 test EIATest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion was Aa, and (∃x)Ax ⊢ Aa is not a valid argument.
problem: {(∃x)Ax=>(∃y)Ay}
2. Aa ; 1 EI
3. (∃y)Ay ; 2 EG
expect: valid

case: ei-a-as-written
source: 2018 test EIATest, as written
problem: {(∃x)Ax=>Aa}
2. Aa ; 1 EI
expect: invalid at 2: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in the conclusion
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine does not check the conclusion when EI picks a constant

case: ei-b
source: 2018 test EIBTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion was Attt, which contains the EI constant.
problem: {(∃y)Ayyy=>(∃x)Axxx}
2. Attt ; 1 EI
3. (∃x)Axxx ; 2 EG
expect: valid

case: ei-b-as-written
source: 2018 test EIBTest, as written
problem: {(∃y)Ayyy=>Attt}
2. Attt ; 1 EI
expect: invalid at 2: EI needs a new constant, and t occurs in the conclusion
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine does not check the conclusion when EI picks a constant

case: ei-c
source: 2018 test EICTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion was Eb, which contains the EI constant.
problem: {Ea & (∃y)Ey=>(∃x)Ex}
2. (∃y)Ey & Ea ; 1 COM
3. (∃y)Ey ; 2 SIMP
4. Eb ; 3 EI
5. (∃x)Ex ; 4 EG
expect: valid

case: ei-c-as-written
source: 2018 test EICTest, as written
problem: {Ea & (∃y)Ey=>Eb}
2. (∃y)Ey & Ea ; 1 COM
3. (∃y)Ey ; 2 SIMP
4. Eb ; 3 EI
expect: invalid at 4: EI needs a new constant, and b occurs in the conclusion
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine does not check the conclusion when EI picks a constant

case: ei-d
source: 2018 test EIDTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion was Eaak, which contains the EI constant k.
problem: {(∃z)((∀x)Exaz & (∃x)Exxz)=>(∃z)Eaaz}
2. (∀x)Exak & (∃x)Exxk ; 1 EI
3. (∀x)Exak ; 2 SIMP
4. Eaak ; 3 UI
5. (∃z)Eaaz ; 4 EG
expect: valid

case: ei-d-as-written
source: 2018 test EIDTest, as written
problem: {(∃z)((∀x)Exaz & (∃x)Exxz)=>Eaak}
2. (∀x)Exak & (∃x)Exxk ; 1 EI
3. (∀x)Exak ; 2 SIMP
4. Eaak ; 3 UI
expect: invalid at 2: EI needs a new constant, and k occurs in the conclusion
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine does not check the conclusion when EI picks a constant

case: ei-e
source: 2018 test EIETest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion was Ejjk, which contains the EI constants j and k.
# Line 2 instantiates a quantifier that binds nothing, so it changes nothing.
problem: {(∃x)((∀x)Waxs & (∃x)(∃z)Exxz)=>(∃z)(∃x)Exxz}
2. (∀x)Waxs & (∃x)(∃z)Exxz ; 1 EI
3. (∃x)(∃z)Exxz & (∀x)Waxs ; 2 COM
4. (∃x)(∃z)Exxz ; 3 SIMP
5. (∃z)Ejjz ; 4 EI
6. Ejjk ; 5 EI
7. (∃x)Exxk ; 6 EG
8. (∃z)(∃x)Exxz ; 7 EG
expect: valid

case: ei-e-as-written
source: 2018 test EIETest, as written
problem: {(∃x)((∀x)Waxs & (∃x)(∃z)Exxz)=>Ejjk}
2. (∀x)Waxs & (∃x)(∃z)Exxz ; 1 EI
3. (∃x)(∃z)Exxz & (∀x)Waxs ; 2 COM
4. (∃x)(∃z)Exxz ; 3 SIMP
5. (∃z)Ejjz ; 4 EI
6. Ejjk ; 5 EI
expect: invalid at 5: EI needs a new constant, and j occurs in the conclusion
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine does not check the conclusion when EI picks a constant

case: ug-a
source: 2018 test UGATest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 premise was Wx & Bx, with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀x)(Wx & Bx)=>(∀x)(Wx)}
2. Wx & Bx ; 1 UI
3. Wx ; 2 SIMP
4. (∀x)(Wx) ; 3 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-a-as-written
source: 2018 test UGATest, as written
problem: {Wx & Bx=>(∀x)(Wx)}
2. Wx ; 1 SIMP
3. (∀x)(Wx) ; 2 UG
expect: invalid at 3: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-b
source: 2018 test UGBTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 premise was Wx & Bx, with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀y)(Wy & By)=>(∀x)(Wx & Bx)}
2. Wx & Bx ; 1 UI
3. (∀x)(Wx & Bx) ; 2 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-b-as-written
source: 2018 test UGBTest, as written
problem: {Wx & Bx=>(∀x)(Wx & Bx)}
2. (∀x)(Wx & Bx) ; 1 UG
expect: invalid at 2: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-c
source: 2018 test UGCTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 premise was Ax, with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀x)Ax=>(∀y)(∀x)(Ax | By)}
2. Ax ; 1 UI
3. Ax | By ; 2 ADD
4. (∀x)(Ax | By) ; 3 UG
5. (∀y)(∀x)(Ax | By) ; 4 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-c-as-written
source: 2018 test UGCTest, as written
problem: {Ax=>(∀y)(∀x)(Ax | By)}
2. Ax | By ; 1 ADD
3. (∀x)(Ax | By) ; 2 UG
4. (∀y)(∀x)(Ax | By) ; 3 UG
expect: invalid at 3: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-d
source: 2018 test UGDTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 premise was Ax, with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀x)Ax=>(∀x)(Bx | Ax)}
2. Ax ; 1 UI
3. Ax | Bx ; 2 ADD
4. Bx | Ax ; 3 COM
5. (∀x)(Bx | Ax) ; 4 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-d-as-written
source: 2018 test UGDTest, as written
problem: {Ax=>(∀x)(Bx | Ax)}
2. Ax | Bx ; 1 ADD
3. Bx | Ax ; 2 COM
4. (∀x)(Bx | Ax) ; 3 UG
expect: invalid at 4: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-e
source: 2018 test UGETest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 premises were Ax | Bx and ~Ax, with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀x)(Ax | Bx)//(∀x)~Ax=>(∀x)Bx}
3. Ax | Bx ; 1 UI
4. ~Ax ; 2 UI
5. Bx ; 3,4 DS
6. (∀x)Bx ; 5 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-e-as-written
source: 2018 test UGETest, as written
problem: {Ax | Bx // ~Ax=>(∀x)Bx}
3. Bx ; 1,2 DS
4. (∀x)Bx ; 3 UG
expect: invalid at 4: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premises 1 and 2
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-f
source: 2018 test UGFTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 first premise was A → ~(Bx & C), with x free, so UG on x was not allowed.
problem: {(∀x)(A → ~(Bx & C))//A & C=>(∀x)~Bx}
3. A → ~(Bx & C) ; 1 UI
4. A ; 2 SIMP
5. ~(Bx & C) ; 3,4 MP
6. ~Bx | ~C ; 5 DM
7. C & A ; 2 COM
8. C ; 7 SIMP
9. ~~C ; 8 DN
10. ~C | ~Bx ; 6 COM
11. ~Bx ; 10,9 DS
12. (∀x)~Bx ; 11 UG
expect: valid

case: ug-f-as-written
source: 2018 test UGFTest, as written
problem: {A → ~(Bx & C) // A & C=>(∀x)~Bx}
3. A ; 2 SIMP
4. ~(Bx & C) ; 1,3 MP
5. ~Bx | ~C ; 4 DM
6. C & A ; 2 COM
7. C ; 6 SIMP
8. ~~C ; 7 DN
9. ~C | ~Bx ; 5 COM
10. ~Bx ; 9,8 DS
11. (∀x)~Bx ; 10 UG
expect: invalid at 11: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-g
source: 2018 test UGGTest, corrected
# Fixed: the 2018 conclusion and line 6 had cx, a typo for Cx.
problem: {(∀x)(Px → Dx)//(∀x)(Dx → Cx)=>(∀x)(Px → Cx)}
3. Py → Dy ; 1 UI
4. Dy → Cy ; 2 UI
5. (Py → Cy) ; 3,4 HS
6. (∀x)(Px → Cx) ; 5 UG
expect: valid
legacy: UG only generalizes the constants a to w, not the variable y

case: ug-h
source: 2018 test UGHTest, corrected
# Fixed: line 3 did EI to the variable y; it now uses the constant a.
problem: {(∀x)(Dx → Cx)//(∃x)(Ax & Dx)=>(∃x)(Ax & Cx)}
3. (Aa & Da) ; 2 EI
4. (Da → Ca) ; 1 UI
5. (Da & Aa) ; 3 COM
6. Da ; 5 SIMP
7. Ca ; 4,6 MP
8. Aa ; 3 SIMP
9. (Aa & Ca) ; 8,7 CONJ
10. (∃x)(Ax & Cx) ; 9 EG
expect: valid

case: ug-h-as-written
source: 2018 test UGHTest, as written
problem: {(∀x)(Dx → Cx)//(∃x)(Ax & Dx)=>(∃x)(Ax & Cx)}
3. (Ay & Dy) ; 2 EI
4. (Dy → Cy) ; 1 UI
5. (Dy & Ay) ; 3 COM
6. Dy ; 5 SIMP
7. Cy ; 4,6 MP
8. Ay ; 3 SIMP
9. (Ay & Cy) ; 8,7 CONJ
10. (∃x)(Ax & Cx) ; 9 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI must use a constant, not the variable y

case: eg-a
source: 2018 test EGATest
problem: {Aa=>((∃x)(Ax))}
2. (∃x)(Ax) ; 1 EG
expect: valid
legacy: the 2018 parser drops the quantifier of (∃x)(Ax) and reads Ax

case: eg-b
source: 2018 test EGBTest
problem: {Ax=>((∃y)(Ay))}
2. (∃y)(Ay) ; 1 EG
expect: valid
legacy: the 2018 parser drops the quantifier of (∃y)(Ay), and EG only generalizes constants

case: eg-c
source: 2018 test EGCTest, Copi exercise 8.6, part II, number 3
problem: {(∃x)(Ax & (∀y)(By → Cxy))//(∃x)Ax → Bj=>(∃x)Cxj}
3. Aa & (∀y)(By → Cay) ; 1 EI
4. Aa ; 3 SIMP
5. (∃x)(Ax) ; 4 EG
6. Bj ; 2,5 MP
7. (∀y)(By → Cay) & Aa ; 3 COM
8. (∀y)(By → Cay) ; 7 SIMP
9. Bj → Caj ; 8 UI
10. Caj ; 6,9 MP
11. (∃x)Cxj ; 10 EG
expect: valid
legacy: the 2018 parser drops the quantifier of (∃x)(Ax) in line 5

case: eg-d
source: 2018 test EGDTest
problem: {(∀y)(Sy → Wy)//(∀y)Sy=>(∃x)Wx}
3. Sy → Wy ; 1 UI
4. Sy ; 2 UI
5. Wy ; 3,4 MP
6. (∃x)Wx ; 5 EG
expect: valid
legacy: EG only generalizes the constants a to w, not the variable y

case: eg-e
source: 2018 test EGETest, corrected
# Fixed: line 3 did EI to the variable y; it now uses the constant a.
problem: {(∀x)(Jx → Kx)//(∃x)(Jx & Lx)=>(∃x)(Lx & Kx)}
3. Ja & La ; 2 EI
4. Ja → Ka ; 1 UI
5. Ja ; 3 SIMP
6. La & Ja ; 3 COM
7. La ; 6 SIMP
8. Ka ; 4,5 MP
9. La & Ka ; 7,8 CONJ
10. (∃x)(Lx & Kx) ; 9 EG
expect: valid

case: eg-e-as-written
source: 2018 test EGETest, as written
problem: {(∀x)(Jx → Kx)//(∃x)(Jx & Lx)=>(∃x)(Lx & Kx)}
3. Jy & Ly ; 2 EI
4. Jy → Ky ; 1 UI
5. Jy ; 3 SIMP
6. Ly & Jy ; 3 COM
7. Ly ; 6 SIMP
8. Ky ; 4,5 MP
9. Ly & Ky ; 7,8 CONJ
10. (∃x)(Lx & Kx) ; 9 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI must use a constant, not the variable y

case: eg-f
source: 2018 test EGFTest, corrected
# Fixed: premise 1 had Aa, a typo for Ax. As written, the argument is not valid.
problem: {(∀x)((Ax | Bx) → Cx)//(∃x)Ax=>(∃x)Cx}
3. Aa ; 2 EI
4. (Aa | Ba) → Ca ; 1 UI
5. Aa | Ba ; 3 ADD
6. Ca ; 4,5 MP
7. (∃x)Cx ; 6 EG
expect: valid

case: eg-f-as-written
source: 2018 test EGFTest, as written
problem: {(∀x)((Aa | Bx) → Cx) //(∃x)Ax=>(∃x)Cx}
3. Aa ; 2 EI
4. (Aa | Ba) → Ca ; 1 UI
5. Aa | Ba ; 3 ADD
6. Ca ; 4,5 MP
7. (∃x)Cx ; 6 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in premise 1
argument: invalid

case: eg-g
source: 2018 test EGGTest, corrected
# Fixed: premise 1 had Aa, a typo for Ax, as in EGFTest.
problem: {(∀x)((Ax | Bx) → Cx)//(∃x)Bx=>(∃x)Cx}
3. Ba ; 2 EI
4. Ba | Aa ; 3 ADD
5. Aa | Ba ; 4 COM
6. (Aa | Ba) → Ca ; 1 UI
7. Ca ; 6,5 MP
8. (∃x)Cx ; 7 EG
expect: valid

case: eg-g-as-written
source: 2018 test EGGTest, as written
problem: {(∀x)((Aa | Bx) → Cx) //(∃x)Bx=>(∃x)Cx}
3. Ba ; 2 EI
4. Ba | Aa ; 3 ADD
5. Aa | Ba ; 4 COM
6. (Aa | Ba) → Ca ; 1 UI
7. Ca ; 6,5 MP
8. (∃x)Cx ; 7 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in premise 1

case: eg-h
source: 2018 test EGHTest
problem: {(∃x)Kx → (∀x)(Lx → Mx)//Kc & Lc =>Mc}
3. Kc ; 2 SIMP
4. (∃x)Kx ; 3 EG
5. (∀x)(Lx → Mx) ; 1,4 MP
6. Lc & Kc ; 2 COM
7. Lc ; 6 SIMP
8. Lc → Mc ; 5 UI
9. Mc ; 8,7 MP
expect: valid
legacy: copied formulas share Constant objects, so EG at line 4 also rewrites line 2 and line 6 fails
